  "definition": "Chemical propulsion converts energy released by a chemical reaction or catalytic decomposition into hot, pressurised gas and then directs that gas through a nozzle to produce thrust. It is used where a spacecraft needs comparatively high thrust or a rapid manoeuvre, provided the available total impulse and the integrated system meet the mission need.[^1]",
